// Title: MSDT Execution Via Answer File
// Sigma ID: 9c8c7000-3065-44a8-a555-79bcba5d9955
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-06-13 | Modified: 2025-10-29
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218, execution
// Description: Detects execution of "msdt.exe" using an answer file which is simulating the legitimate way of
//   calling msdt via "pcwrun.exe" (For example from the compatibility tab).
// False positives:
//   - Possible undocumented parents of "msdt" other than "pcwrun".
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Msdt/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_msdt_answer_file_exec.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\msdt.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\WINDOWS\\diagnostics\\index\\PCWDiagnostic.xml" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -af " or ProcessCommandLine contains " /af " or ProcessCommandLine contains " –af " or ProcessCommandLine contains " —af " or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―af ")) and (not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\pcwrun.exe"))
